brush is a shell written in Rust that implements POSIX shell behavior
and a large subset of Bash.  It is intended to run existing scripts and
.bashrc files, and includes an interactive line editor with syntax
highlighting, history and programmable completion.

This package installs the shell as ${PREFIX}/bin/brush and registers it
in /etc/shells.  It is not installed as a bash(1) replacement: the
package provides no ${PREFIX}/bin/bash and neither conflicts with nor
claims shells/bash.

brush is not a complete Bash implementation: select, wait -n, disown
and logout are not implemented, signal traps are still in progress, and
there are known edge cases in IFS splitting, printf and alias
expansion.  Upstream maintains a compatibility reference at
https://github.com/reubeno/brush/blob/main/docs/reference/compatibility.md
and validates the shell against bash with a large compatibility test
suite.
